# Samsung proprietary firmware blobs staged for boot probes — NEVER commit.
#
# These are extracted from the device's own firmware and are redistributable to
# nobody. They live here because the probe initramfs needs them at build time,
# not because they belong in history.
#
# This rule exists because a `git add -A` run from inside the kernel tree staged
# 8.3 MB of them (a740_sqe.fw, a740_zap.mbn, regulatory.db) in one go. It was
# caught by reading the staged list before committing — which is not a control,
# it is luck. The parent repo's .gitignore has a "Firmware blobs — Samsung
# proprietary, NEVER commit" block, but its rules do not reach inside this
# nested repository, so the policy was unenforced exactly here.
firmware/
